# Dallas Arbiter Fuzz Face Hardware Specs
# Reference: 1966 Germanium PNP original circuit
#
# Classic germanium Fuzz Face uses AC128 or NKT275 PNP transistors.
# This file lets `check_voltage_with_specs()` flag real problems
# when you crank the supply past 9V.
#
# Enable with: cargo build --features hardware

# Germanium PNP transistors - matched pair recommended
# AC128, NKT275, or OC44 are period-correct
# Note: Ge transistors are temperature sensitive
Q1: vce_max(32) part("AC128")
Q2: vce_max(32) part("AC128")

# Input coupling - non-polarized or bipolar electrolytic
C1: voltage_rating(25) part("2.2uF Electrolytic")

# Emitter bypass - enhances gain
C2: voltage_rating(25) part("20uF Electrolytic")

# Output coupling
C3: voltage_rating(25) part("10nF Film")

# Standard 1/4W resistors
R1: power_rating(0.25)
R2: power_rating(0.25)
R3: power_rating(0.25)
R4: power_rating(0.25)

# Pots
Fuzz: part("1k Linear")
Volume: part("500k Log")
